    ]
  },
  "summary": {
    "en": [
      "Eugene Bak Gene Bak was born in Poland. In February 1940 the Soviets deported his entire village, including his family to Siberia. His family escaped from Siberia in 1942 and went to Uzbekistan where his father joined the Polish Army in Exile. The army and their civilian families were evacuated from the Soviet Union to Iran in August 1942. As a young child Gene spent five years in Polish refugee camps in Iran, Pakistan, and India."
    ]
  },
